# Lisp source is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# NOT a tidiness preference.  FORMAT's line-continuation directive is a tilde followed
# by a NEWLINE, and this codebase uses it heavily to keep long control strings
# readable.  Where git converts to CRLF on checkout, that becomes tilde-CR, which is
# not a directive at all -- so a Windows build fails at COMPILE-FILE with
#
#   error in FORMAT: Unknown directive (character: Return)
#
# pointing into a string that is perfectly correct in the repository.  The file is
# fine; the checkout was not.
*.lisp   text eol=lf
*.asd    text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
